codex
The status evidence is decisive: all 912 records at `(status=3, extended_status=3)` are future-due, while every `extended_status=0` record—including 673 at status 3—is overdue. I’m therefore treating status 3 as the full learned tier, with `extended_status=3` as its durable-known subset; one contradictory `(status=0, extended_status=3)` row is flagged and excluded from the learned lexicons. This preserves both the nominal meaning and the stronger account-specific known signal.
