codex
The overlap is much smaller than the raw estate size suggests: across the five product languages, only 11 of 1,248 learned terms appear in either current corpus, leaving 1,237 dormant (99.12%). Nearly all of that value is single-word vocabulary (1,231 terms); only 6 learned multi-word terms are dormant, so the strongest near-term use is personalized vocabulary constraints and reactivation—not a large known-idiom library. I’m encoding that distinction explicitly in the report.
